  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPROVED SECURITY AND MONITORING OF THE KEY 1 BLACK RHINO POPULATION IN THE TSAVO WEST NATIONAL PARK S INTENSIVE PROTECTION ZONE, SOUTHERN KENYA IN LINE WITH THE NATIONAL RHINO STRATEGY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT A CONSERVATION EFFORT IN TSAVO WEST NATIONAL PARK, KENYA BY ENHANCING SECURITY, CONDUCTING MONITORING, AND SUPPORTING PARK MANAGEMENT TO CONSERVE THE EASTERN BLACK RHINOCEROS AND THEIR HABITAT. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO ENHANCE KENYA S EASTERN BLACK RHINOCEROS POPULATION GROWTH BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF POACHING AND THE NEED FOR BIOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) PROVIDING EQUIPMENT AND RESOURCES FOR AERIAL AND GROUND PROTECTION (2) MONITORING TO INDIVIDUALLY IDENTIFY AND REGULARLY CHECK ON THE BLACK RHINOCEROS POPULATION AND (3) CONDUCTING BIOLOGICAL MANAGEMENT TO ALLOW FOR CONTINUED POPULATION GROWTH.</narrative>
  </description>
